#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046668} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565517} :activity/id #uuid "71a8b3cb-fa15-5adb-be3d-13c0443f9e35" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048778 :topic/id #uuid "bdf6a63d-1183-5d54-9223-faab1de59819" :topic/math-academy-id 60} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565487 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564969} {:answer/id #uuid "40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565033} {:answer/id #uuid "577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∧R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565203} {:answer/id #uuid "f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565305}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :question/math-academy-id "q-177452" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}$ is rational, **or** $3|12$ **and** $3|18.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $Q:3|12$\n\n- $R:3|18\\text{ }$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\sqrt{5}$ is rational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3|12$ and $3|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3|12}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3|18}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∧R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3|12\\text{ and }3|18}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∧R).$"} :step/id #uuid "0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565516}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565516 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} {:answer/id #uuid "56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565035} :answer-field/id #uuid "1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} {:answer/id #uuid "addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565197}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564958} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565246} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565311} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :question/math-academy-id "q-178163" :question/problem "$$\n{{0\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{1\\}=\\{1,2\\}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ is irrational}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, but the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∨\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565538}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565517 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc55069c-667c-5e08-b2b0-341a1b91bc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∨(S∨T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051753} {:answer/id #uuid "d4920408-8a32-5926-8964-f320c3ee7ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∨(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} {:answer/id #uuid "d8af7fc3-5f6b-5139-9b22-d82aba7b2766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(R∨S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051755} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eff23a-ece4-5063-9fd2-b91ca4789a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R∧(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051756} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d624ca-e16c-5795-906f-04ab06d6cdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(R∧S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4759e44-79a1-5658-a783-9ae9824ce60b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c3a7db47-e883-5a71-8bfd-ec843bd98b41" :question/math-academy-id "q-170852" :question/problem "$2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R:2\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $S:14\\text{ is a multiple of }7$\n\n- $T:14\\text{ is a multiple of }5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$"} :step/id #uuid "8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565537}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565537 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398dfebf-2715-5754-8536-2fbf57b13ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379007} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbd595e-8862-5ddd-ad65-9bbe8a1503d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379008}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379008} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73e4d24-a544-5df8-926d-0dd2efcec4c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7724fa1-404c-5cf6-a1e4-ffe8e50a65bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379010} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b3e6af-d78b-5785-9381-3f1554e4df26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379011} :answer-field/id #uuid "8de5b0f9-3915-5928-8eee-ebfbdd12e385" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e7d887d-e0e7-5390-878c-560d04e1e11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379013} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1049a9-d8a0-54f8-b526-d6d1108f314b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379013} :answer-field/id #uuid "576ab971-a207-5967-8d37-5db8a4c60c7d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b8a204fe-0678-5217-8fd6-73d54f821b1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-175909" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{2}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{1-2=1}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565487}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565538 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4e9e86-8284-5124-a5d8-2986c678430f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051966} {:answer/id #uuid "351e3b6e-328b-51b3-a3b4-654ed5082185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f130160-11dc-5d3a-9856-5fbf9e017de3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a784ae67-278a-5990-a46b-9305f5e46ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} {:answer/id #uuid "ec33348b-a0de-5fdb-82f8-56f288950968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f5e149-319b-5aca-8113-65c296ae9284" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0974b375-a54a-5d5e-846e-11f8487271d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051972} {:answer/id #uuid "40bf36f3-987d-514b-a937-3a85bd10e5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf02d32-be98-53f4-bb26-71699b829f9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "251d1784-5e7a-5d2b-9609-81be8de6d435" :question/math-academy-id "q-181713" :question/problem "$$\n{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b"}] :activity/title "The \"And\" and \"Or\" Connectives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564930}]}
